  "method": "Long Island (with Conception Island and Dean's Blue Hole), Rum Cay, San Salvador, Cat Island, Great Inagua, and Crooked and Acklins Islands. No official site list exists; Bahamas National Trust pages for Conception Island and Inagua name no dive sites. Lists used: the tourism list (Bahamas Ministry of Tourism dive page and island pages together with the My Out Islands pages for Long Island, San Salvador, Cat Island and the other islands, counted as one list); Stella Maris Resort (Long Island; read from the 2011 Wayback snapshot of its dive-locations page, as the current page lists only Comberbach, Conception and Dean's); Cape Santa Maria Beach Resort (Long Island); Riding Rock Resort and Marina (San Salvador); Only Blue Diving, the Club Med Columbus Isle dive center (San Salvador, a separate operator); and Hawk's Nest Resort (Cat Island, 2018 Wayback snapshot; its current site no longer offers diving). Greenwood Beach Resort and Fernandez Bay Village (Cat Island) publish no site names, and no operator list exists for Rum Cay, Great Inagua, Crooked Island or Acklins, so those islands contribute nothing to the count beyond HMS Conqueror. Cat Island has two lists with no site in common, so every Cat Island site is excluded as one list only. A site counts when named, recreationally divable on scuba and on at least two lists. Dean's Blue Hole is counted because two Long Island resorts sell it as a scuba trip, though it is mainly a freediving venue. Counted 2026-10-14.",
